  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-08-26T14:24:18.147Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "In Unity editor, If you select several GameObjects holding VRC_Trigger and proceed editing, you'll get meaningless result.\n\nFor example:\n1. Create a Cube,   Add VRC_Trigger, Add  OnEnterTrigger trigger, Set broadcast type AlwaysUnbuffered, Set Layers as Environment\n2. Create a Sphere, Add VRC_Trigger, Add OnEnterCollider trigger, Set broadcast type AlwaysBufferOne, Set Layers as PlayerLocal\n3. Select the Cube, and ctrl+click Sphere to begin multi-object editing.\n4. Change Material in Mesh Renderer component.\n5. Select another object to end multi-object editing.\n6. Open inspector of the Cube, you'll see OnEnterCollider trigger, AlwaysBufferOne, Layers as Environment. it is changed.\n\nI think, editting other component should not affect VRC_Trigger.\nAnd also it is not copy operation. Trigger type and broadcast type are copyed, but Layers is left. Totally, it's meaningless.\n\nI think CanEditMultipleObjects Attribute (https://docs.unity3d.com/ScriptReference/CanEditMultipleObjects.html) of class VRC_TriggerEditor (VRCSDK/Dependencies/VRChat/Editor/VRC_TriggerEditor.cs) should be removed.",
  "error": null,
